pkgcheck_result(3)

# NAME

pkgcheck_result - seal terminal package check evidence

# SYNOPSIS

```
auto passed = pkgcheck::check_result::passed(request, execution);
auto failed = pkgcheck::check_result::failed(
    request, execution, failure_kind, failure_evidence);
```

# DESCRIPTION

A passed result binds one exact check request to typed execution evidence. A
failed result additionally binds one failure classification and typed failure
evidence.

The core does not interpret process status or backend diagnostics. That mapping
belongs to the execution adapter.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgcheck*(3), *pkgcheck_request*(3)
